task: losing-rows
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/losing-rows
worktree: ../okay-wt-perf

why: after schedulers-family, three things in §4b are unfinished and
  each has a number attached:
  1. CANCEL: we read 1089 us for 1 000 parked fibers against cats'
     692 and ZIO's 786, and §4b says why — our cancel is a thread
     interrupt, theirs is a flag a fiber checks. But `Schedulers.own`
     cancels a DriveTask by SETTING A FLAG (`Drive.stopped`), no
     thread involved. The row was never measured on it.
  2. MANY-TO-MANY: 4964 against ZIO's 3122 with the ring, and the
     partitioned buffer reads 2502 — but it is opt-in because of a
     rare P x C deadlock (`adaptive-p-x-c-deadlock`), which is
     therefore the thing standing between us and that row.
  3. the Chase-Lev deque's own contribution is UNMEASURED (landed
     while the wake defect masked everything).

what:
  1. cancel1k lanes on `Schedulers.own` and `.adaptive`, measured
     beside the existing okay/zio/cats rows in one run.
  2. hunt the P x C deadlock: a stress harness at the shape the JMH
     fork hung at (4x4, thousands of rounds) plus the timed-park
     diagnosis that cracked the seal race; then fix, then re-measure
     the many-to-many row with the adaptive buffer.
  3. an A/B of the deque against a per-worker queue, recorded either
     way.

predict:
  1. cancel on `own` under 400 us: no unpark, no InterruptedException,
     no unwind — a CAS on a cell and the join's callback. If it lands
     between 600 and 800 the cost was never the interrupt and §4b's
     explanation is wrong, which is worth knowing.
  2. the deadlock is `wakeSender()` waking `sendersAt(ring.lastRoute)`
     — the part last POPPED, not the part the parked sender is
     waiting on. Disqualifying: a dump showing the parked sender's
     route equal to lastRoute.
  3. the deque is worth 0-10% and the honest answer may be "nothing";
     recorded either way.
